    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47475" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tanūsius</span></b> , ii,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				name of a Roman</i> gens: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tanusiorum capita demere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Q.
						Cic. Pet. Cons. 2, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp.: Tanusius Geminus, <i>a Latin historian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annales Tanusii scis quam ponderosi sint,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 93, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 9</span></i>.</div>
